        "original_id": "6200d8ff-eae3-58e1-958f-f5dd332f46d1",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Philip Seymour Hoffman, Amy Adams, Joseph Foster\n- Films: Doubt (2008 film)\n- Characters: Sister James, Sister Aloysius, Father Flynn, Donald Miller\n- Topics: acting career, plot events\n\nFacts:\n- Philip Seymour Hoffman was born on July 23, 1967.\n- Philip Seymour Hoffman was an American actor, director, and producer.\n- Philip Seymour Hoffman was best known for distinctive supporting and character roles, often portraying lowlifes, eccentrics, bullies, and misfits.\n- Philip Seymour Hoffman acted in many films from the early 1990s until his death.\n- In Doubt (2008 film), Sister James, played by Amy Adams, tells Sister Aloysius that Father Flynn, played by Philip Seymour Hoffman, might be giving too much personal attention to Donald Miller, the school’s only Black student, played by Joseph Foster.\n- In Doubt (2008 film), Sister Aloysius begins a crusade against Father Flynn after Sister James raises her concern about Donald Miller.\n- Philip Seymour Hoffman died on February 2, 2014, at age 46.",
